.TH GIT-REPO-STATE 1 "2026-06-14" "git-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-repo-state \- report repository workflow state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git repo-state
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git repo-state
prints a read-only repository state report: current branch, inferred default
branch, upstream divergence, dirty worktree counts, active operation, stash
count, and current branch pull request details when GitHub data is available.
.PP
The command does not require GitHub access. If
.B gh
is unavailable or unauthenticated, local repository state is still reported and
pull request fields are left empty.
.PP
When GitHub data is available, view and checks queries are pinned to the current
checkout repository rather than ambient GitHub CLI routing.
.PP
When GitHub refuses the token the pull request's checks, they are read through
the Actions API, as in
.BR git-pr-land (1).
Check runs from apps other than GitHub Actions are then invisible, and this
report has no merge-state gate to catch them: a pull request whose only
failing or pending checks come from such an app can read as passing, unless
GitHub reports its merge state
.BR UNSTABLE ,
which reads as pending.
.PP
The repository identity lookup is cached for one hour under
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME/git-tools/repo-identity
(or
.B ~/.cache
when unset). Entries are keyed by the repository path and its configured
remotes, so renaming the checkout or editing remotes invalidates the cache
immediately; only successful lookups are cached.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-porcelain
Print stable
.B key=value
output for scripts.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a flat JSON object.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
State printed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or local environment error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-pr-checks (1),
.BR git-cleanup-repo (1)
